WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:02.054
The mouse is sniffing around for a meal.

00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:09.689
He'll eat almost anything, but prefers
seeds, nuts and vegetation.

00:00:14.236 --> 00:00:20.100
Like all mice, he feels safer near
vertical surfaces, rocks, grass and trees.

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:22.662
It maximises his escape options.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.246
This little guy is an excellent all-round
athlete.

00:00:27.886 --> 00:00:30.768
He can run, climb, jump and swim.

00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:35.635
A juicy crop of lush green seedlings.

00:00:36.596 --> 00:00:41.561
The food has attracted a range of small
hungry mammals, and the small mammals have

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:42.822
attracted something else.

00:00:43.863 --> 00:00:44.704
A barn owl.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.468
The mouse is unaware of her presence.

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:53.292
Owls have acute hearing and can move in
absolute silence.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.315
But the mouse is well camouflaged.

00:00:57.764 --> 00:00:58.985
The owl is on the prowl.

00:01:00.205 --> 00:01:04.447
Her soft wings carry her through the
forest as she scans the undergrowth.

00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:08.049
The mouse is hard to spot, but not
impossible.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.190
His race is over.

00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:15.452
This tiger snake has highly sensitive
smell.

00:01:16.693 --> 00:01:19.614
The darkness is not a problem when you're
relying on smell.

00:01:20.855 --> 00:01:22.216
The mouse can smell something.

00:01:23.976 --> 00:01:27.017
Mice are born knowing which smells signal
danger.

00:01:28.678 --> 00:01:33.119
Now the mouse has no choice but to keep
still, wait and hope he hasn't been

00:01:33.179 --> 00:01:33.879
noticed.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.721
But the snake is onto him.

00:01:38.961 --> 00:01:41.342
The mouse has a very unwelcome guest.

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.063
He's trapped.

00:01:43.863 --> 00:01:45.424
It's game over for the mouse.

